"Derivative Work" means any work that incorporates, is derived from, or
builds upon the Software, including Modifications.

"Distribute" means to make the Software or a Derivative Work available
to any third party, whether by transfer of copies, publication of source
code, provision as a hosted or managed service, or any other means.

"Community Use" means use of the Software in a production environment
managing no more than five (5) hosted domains or websites simultaneously.

"Commercial Use" means any production use of the Software that exceeds
the limits of Community Use, including managing more than five (5) hosted
domains or websites.

"Competing Product" means any software product, platform, or service that
provides web hosting control panel functionality to third parties,
including but not limited to: management of multiple hosted domains or
websites on behalf of customers, automated web server configuration for
multiple tenants, containerized workload deployment for hosting customers,
multi-tenant hosting account management, or SFTP/SSH access provisioning
for hosting customers. Existing products such as cPanel, DirectAdmin,
Plesk, and Froxlor are examples of Competing Products.

"License Enforcement Mechanisms" means any code, configuration, or
technical controls within the Software that verify license keys, count
hosted domains or sites, enforce domain or feature limits, report usage
statistics to the Licensor's servers, or restrict access to functionality
based on license tier.


